::kind(api)

::meta(crate: sisho-board-core, dependencies: (sisho-board-sdk), dependents: (sisho-board))

=[sisho-board-core]

The operating dashboard and board for the Tomet ecosystem (`sisho-board`).

Two-tier design:

- @strong[Board]: Status of tools, extensions (with explicit user trust via `~/.config/sisho/board.json`),

extension board panes (`--sisho-board-pane`), integrity check outcomes, and broken links.

- @strong[Counter]: Action prompt bar to run check, fix, check-links, toggle extension trust, or open desk.

==[Module editor]

Editor resolution for opening broken link files from `sisho-board`.

===[Functions]

====[fn resolve_editor]

Resolve an editor command to open `file` at `line`.

Precedence chain:
1. `$SISHO_EDITOR` (handles `{file}`, `{line}`, `{col}` templates, allowed extension words, or commands)
2. `$VISUAL` (Unix full-screen editor: nvim, vim, hx, etc.)
3. `$EDITOR` (Unix standard editor)
4. `sisho-desk` (if installed, active, and \[`TrustState::Allowed`\])
5. `nano` (system fallback)

====[fn resolve_editor_with_lookup]

==[Module extension]

Extension discovery and protocol querying (`--sisho-extension-info` and `--sisho-board-pane`).

Security boundary: \[`scan`\] and \[`scan_in`\] only inspect directory entries
and file permissions on `PATH`; they never execute any discovered program.
\[`query_info`\] and \[`query_board_pane`\] must only be called for extensions
whose \[`TrustState`\] is \[`TrustState::Allowed`\].

===[Functions]

====[fn is_valid_word]

True if `word` is a valid extension name (`[a-z0-9-]+`, not starting with `-`).

====[fn scan]

Scan `PATH` for `sisho-<word>` extension executables (excluding `sisho-board` itself).

Never executes any discovered binary. All returned items start with
\[`TrustState::Untrusted`\]; the caller applies \[`crate::trust::TrustConfig`\]
before deciding whether any extension may be queried.

====[fn scan_in]

Scan specific directories for `sisho-<word>` extension executables.

====[fn query_info]

Query an allowed extension executable for its `--sisho-extension-info` metadata.

====[fn query_board_pane]

Query an allowed extension executable for its `--sisho-board-pane <dir>` data.

==[Module links]

The link check as the board shows it: what `tomet check-links --json`
reports about the links of a vault that point at nothing.

===[Structs]

====[struct Position]

A line and a column, both counted from 1.

====[struct BrokenLink]

A link whose target does not exist.

====[struct Unreadable]

A document that could not be looked at.

====[struct Report]

What a run found.

===[Functions]

====[fn check]

Check the links under `dir` by running `tomet check-links --json`.

==[Module model]

State model and background worker coordination for `sisho-board`.

===[Structs]

====[struct ExtensionItem]

An extension discovered on `PATH` and presented on the Board.

====[struct ToolStatus]

Status of a core ecosystem tool (`tomet`, `twrit`, `catasto`).

====[struct ExtensionPaneItemRef]

Reference to a single item inside an allowed extension's \[`BoardPane`\].

====[struct Model]

The state of the board and counter.

===[Enums]

====[enum StepSlot]

A slot representing a check or fix step in progress or completed.

====[enum FocusedPane]

The currently focused pane on the Board.

====[enum PreviewSource]

Which pane provides the content currently shown in the Output Preview pane.

====[enum WorkerMessage]

Messages sent from background worker threads to the model.

==[Module runner]

Subprocess runner and parallel job execution for `sisho-board`.

===[Structs]

====[struct Step]

A command ready to be run.

====[struct Outcome]

What a single step produced.

===[Enums]

====[enum Status]

How a step ended.

===[Functions]

====[fn init_gate]

Initialize the process-wide jobserver gate.

====[fn run_parallel_streaming]

Run `steps` in parallel and invoke `on_complete(index, outcome)` as each step finishes.
Returns the outcomes in their original plan order.

====[fn run_with_timeout]

Run a program with arguments and a timeout, returning `Some(stdout)` if it exits 0 within `timeout`.

==[Module screen]

Terminal guard: manages raw mode, alternate screen, and mouse capture.

===[Structs]

====[struct Screen]

Terminal guard: ensures terminal is restored to normal state even on panic or error.

===[Functions]

====[fn restore_terminal]

Restore the terminal to cooked mode and exit alternate screen. Safe to call multiple times.

==[Module tools]

Core ecosystem tools (`tomet`, `twrit`, `catasto`) and plans inspected by `sisho-board`.

===[Structs]

====[struct Version]

A semantic version `(major, minor, patch)`.

===[Enums]

====[enum Verdict]

How a tool's reported version compares against its minimum required version.

====[enum Tool]

A core tool in the Tomet ecosystem.

===[Functions]

====[fn check_steps]

The steps of `sisho check` for `path`.

====[fn fix_steps]

The steps of `sisho fix` for `path`.

====[fn check_links_step]

`tomet check-links --json <path>`.

==[Module trust]

User trust configuration (`~/.config/sisho/board.json`).

By default, discovered extensions on `PATH` are \[`TrustState::Untrusted`\].
`sisho-board` never executes an extension subprocess (`--sisho-extension-info`,
`--sisho-board-pane`, editor launch, or terminal handover) unless the user
has explicitly marked it \[`TrustState::Allowed`\].

===[Structs]

====[struct TrustConfig]

Persistent trust configuration stored at `~/.config/sisho/board.json`.

===[Enums]

====[enum TrustState]

Trust permission state for an extension discovered on `PATH`.

===[Functions]

====[fn default_config_path]

Resolve the default path to `board.json`:
`$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/sisho/board.json` if `XDG_CONFIG_HOME` is set and non-empty,
otherwise `$HOME/.config/sisho/board.json`.

====[fn resolve_config_path_with]

Resolve the path to `board.json` using a custom environment variable lookup function.

===[Constants]

====[const CURRENT_TRUST_SCHEMA_VERSION]

Current schema version for `board.json`.

==[Module ui]

Ratatui rendering for `sisho-board` (Board + Counter).

===[Functions]

====[fn draw]

Render the complete sisho-board interface (Board + Counter).

==[Functions]

===[fn run]

Run the interactive board TUI in `dir`.

===[fn run_with_extensions]

Run the interactive board TUI in `dir` with pre-scanned `extensions`.
